---
/**
 * Privacy policy — DRAFT (compliance scope, CLAUDE.md).
 *
 * Status: DRAFT — placeholders in [BRACKETS] must be completed by the operator
 * and the whole page MUST be reviewed by a qualified lawyer before launch
 * (CLAUDE.md: privacy/cookie/terms are draft-only until human lawyer review;
 * never present as a final legal document). Do NOT remove the draft banner
 * until lawyer sign-off is recorded in DECISIONS.md.
 *
 * Grounded in the ACTUAL data handling of this site (do not embellish):
 * - Intake answers live ONLY in the visitor's browser localStorage
 *   (key `relocation-intake-v2`); never transmitted to our servers; no accounts.
 * - Share links encode an allowlist of plan-shaping answers in the URL FRAGMENT
 *   (after `#`), which browsers never send to servers; free text is never encoded.
 * - Launch waitlist (routes not live yet): the email/phone a visitor optionally
 *   submits are stored on-device (`rg-waitlist-v1`) and, DORMANT BY DEFAULT, are
 *   NOT transmitted. They are sent off-device only if PUBLIC_WAITLIST_ENDPOINT is
 *   configured, and only with the visitor's explicit, unticked consent. Payload
 *   is coarse (route + motivation + contact) — never free text. Before enabling,
 *   this section + the controller/processor details must be lawyer-reviewed.
 * - Analytics (PLANNED, ADR-0004): Plausible (cookieless) primary + GA4 behind a
 *   consent gate. Advertising (PLANNED, post-launch): Google AdSense behind the
 *   same consent gate. None are active yet — the site has no production domain.
 *
 * Regulatory scope (verify with counsel): GDPR, Swiss revised FADP, UK GDPR /
 * PECR, CCPA / CPRA, Canada PIPEDA, Brazil LGPD.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy — Relocation Guide"
  description="How Relocation Guide handles your data: intake answers stay in your browser; analytics and advertising run only with your consent."
>
  <!-- DRAFT banner — remove only after human lawyer sign-off -->
  <aside
    role="note"
    aria-label="Draft status"
    class="rounded-md border border-rose-300 bg-rose-50 p-4 text-sm text-rose-900"
  >
    <p>
      <strong>DRAFT — not yet in force.</strong> This policy contains placeholder values
      in [BRACKETS] and has not been reviewed by a lawyer. It must not be treated as a
      final legal document until the operator details are completed and a qualified
      lawyer has approved the wording for every jurisdiction we serve.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <article class="prose prose-slate mt-8 max-w-2xl space-y-8">
    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="text-slate-600">
        This policy explains what data Relocation Guide ("we", "us") collects, why, and
        the choices you have. The short version: <strong>the answers you give the
        planner stay in your own browser</strong> &mdash; we do not run accounts and do
        not receive them on our servers.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">
        Operator and contact details are in our <a href="/impressum">Impressum</a>.
        Cookie and local-storage specifics are in our
        <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie policy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Who is responsible (controller)</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        The data controller for this website is [OPERATOR NAME], [STREET ADDRESS,
        POSTCODE, CITY, COUNTRY]. Contact: [CONTACT EMAIL]. Where we determine the
        purposes and means of processing, we act as controller under the GDPR, the
        Swiss revised Federal Act on Data Protection (FADP), and the other laws listed
        below.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Your planner answers stay in your browser</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        When you use the relocation planner, your answers &mdash; origin and destination
        country, passports you hold, your reason for moving, family and study or work
        details, whether children are moving with you, and your progress through the
        checklist &mdash; are saved <strong>only in your own browser's local storage</strong>
        (a small store the browser keeps on your device, under the key
        <code>relocation-intake-v2</code>). This data:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-slate-700">
        <li>is <strong>not transmitted to our servers</strong> and is not stored by us;</li>
        <li>is not linked to an account &mdash; we do not offer accounts or logins;</li>
        <li>stays on your device until you clear it (see "Your choices" below).</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        Because this data never reaches us, we cannot retrieve, export, or delete it for
        you &mdash; but you can do all three yourself at any time from your browser.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Sharing a plan by link</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        If you copy a link to your plan, the plan-shaping answers are encoded in the part
        of the URL after the <code>#</code> symbol (the "fragment"). By web standard,
        browsers <strong>never send the fragment to any server</strong> &mdash; not to
        ours, and not in the address bar's network request. Free-text entries are never
        included in a share link. Anyone you send the link to can reconstruct the plan in
        their own browser, so only share it with people you choose.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Launch waitlist (routes that aren't live yet)</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        We add relocation routes one at a time, after independent fact-checking. If your route
        isn't live yet, you can ask us to tell you when it launches by giving an
        <strong>email address (and, optionally, a phone number)</strong>. This is entirely
        optional &mdash; you never have to provide it to use the planner.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-slate-700">
        <li>
          We ask for <strong>explicit, opt-in consent</strong> (an unticked box) before you submit,
          and we use the details for <strong>one purpose only</strong>: to notify you about that
          one route. No newsletters, no sharing, no other use.
        </li>
        <li>
          What we would store with your contact details is <strong>coarse</strong>: the route
          (origin and destination) and your stated reason for moving &mdash; <strong>never</strong>
          your free-text entries (employer, institution, "other" description).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>[Current default: off-device sending is not yet enabled.]</strong> Until we
          connect and disclose a notification provider, a signup is stored only in your own
          browser (<code>rg-waitlist-v1</code>) and is not transmitted to us. When we enable
          sending, this section will be updated with the provider, retention period, and your
          rights, and reviewed by a lawyer first.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Special-category data</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        Some answers can reveal sensitive information &mdash; for example, indicating a
        registered partnership may imply data about your relationships, which the GDPR
        treats as a "special category" (Art. 9). We collect this <strong>only to tailor
        the checklist</strong>, it is processed entirely within your browser as described
        above, and it is never sent to us. We ask for the minimum needed to show the
        right steps.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Analytics</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        [PLANNED &mdash; activates at launch.] To understand which guidance is useful, we
        intend to use:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-slate-700">
        <li>
          <strong>Plausible Analytics</strong> &mdash; a privacy-friendly, cookieless
          measurement tool that does not collect personal data or track you across sites.
          Because it sets no cookies and processes no personal data, it runs without a
          consent prompt, in our legitimate interest in maintaining the site.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Analytics 4 (GA4)</strong> &mdash; loaded <strong>only if you
          give consent</strong> via our cookie banner. GA4 uses cookies and may transfer
          data to Google. If you do not consent, GA4 is not loaded.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        Any analytics events we record describe actions (for example, "advanced a step"
        or "opened an official form link") using coarse categories only. They do
        <strong>not</strong> include your free-text entries, the passports you listed,
        employer or institution names, or anything that identifies you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Advertising</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        [PLANNED &mdash; post-launch.] We may display ads through Google AdSense to help
        fund the site. If we do, ad cookies and personalised advertising will load
        <strong>only with your consent</strong> via the cookie banner, and never
        alongside legal or visa guidance, document checklists, or official-source links.
        You can withdraw consent at any time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Server logs and hosting</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        Our host ([HOSTING PROVIDER &mdash; e.g. Cloudflare Pages]) may process standard
        technical request data (such as IP address and user-agent) to deliver the site
        securely and to defend against abuse. This is necessary to operate the website
        and is handled under the host's own data-processing terms. [Confirm retention and
        the data-processing agreement with the host before launch.]
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Legal bases (GDPR / UK GDPR / FADP)</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-slate-700">
        <li>
          <strong>Operating the planner in your browser</strong> &mdash; strictly
          necessary to provide the service you requested (Art. 6(1)(b)); the data does not
          reach us.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cookieless analytics and secure hosting</strong> &mdash; our legitimate
          interests in running and improving the site (Art. 6(1)(f)).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Consent-based analytics and advertising</strong> &mdash; your consent
          (Art. 6(1)(a); and Art. 9(2)(a) for any special-category processing),
          withdrawable at any time.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Your choices and rights</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-slate-700">
        <li>
          <strong>Clear your planner data</strong> at any time using the planner's
          "Start over" control, or by clearing this site's data in your browser settings.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Change or withdraw consent</strong> for analytics and advertising at any
          time from the cookie settings link in the footer.
        </li>
        <li>
          Under the GDPR, UK GDPR, FADP, CCPA/CPRA, PIPEDA, and LGPD you may have rights to
          access, correct, delete, port, or object to processing, and to lodge a complaint
          with a supervisory authority. Because planner answers never reach us, the
          fastest way to exercise access/deletion over them is directly in your browser; for
          anything we do process (e.g. host logs), contact us at [CONTACT EMAIL].
        </li>
        <li>
          [California] We do not sell or share personal information as defined by the
          CCPA/CPRA. [Confirm with counsel.]
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">International transfers</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        If you consent to GA4 or AdSense, data may be transferred to Google outside your
        country (including the United States) under the transfer mechanisms Google relies
        on. Cookieless analytics and the in-browser planner involve no such transfer by
        us. [Confirm transfer mechanisms with counsel before launch.]
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Children</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        This site is intended for adults planning a relocation. It is not directed at
        children, and we do not knowingly collect data from children. (The planner asks
        whether children are relocating with you only to show the right steps; that answer
        stays in your browser.)
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        We may update this policy as the site evolves (for example, when analytics or ads
        go live). Material changes will be reflected here with a new "last updated" date.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">
      Last updated: [DATE — set when placeholders are filled in]. Draft pending human
      lawyer review.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
